The Lost City of Z is a 2016 American epic biographical adventure drama film written and
directed by James Gray, based on the 2009 book of the same name by David Grann.

12
01:16:54,545 --> 01:17:00,545
It portrays British explorer Percy Fawcett, who was sent to Brazil and made
several attempts to find a supposed ancient lost city in the Amazon.

13
01:23:19,090 --> 01:23:25,090
It stars Charlie Hunnam as Fawcett; Robert Pattinson as his fellow explorer Henry Costin,
Sienna Miller as his wife, Nina Fawcett; and Tom Holland as his son, Jack.

14
01:29:43,636 --> 01:29:49,636
Its world premiere was on October 15, 2016, as the
closing-night selection at the New York Film Festival.

15
01:36:08,181 --> 01:36:14,181
It was released in the United States on April 14, 2017
by Amazon Studios and Bleecker Street.

16
01:42:32,727 --> 01:42:38,727
It was praised by critics, but grossed only $19
million against a $30 million budget.

17
01:48:57,272 --> 01:49:03,272
